# Punctuation: no em dashes or en dashes

Do not use em dashes (`—`, U+2014) or en dashes (`–`, U+2013) in any user-facing text (UI, metadata, alt text, buttons, tables).

Use instead:
- **Comma** for appositives: `Japan, not a travel agency`
- **Period** for separate sentences: `Plan your trip first. Each guide opens in one click.`
- **Colon** for titles or labels: `Japan Itinerary (7 Days): First-Time Guide`
- **Hyphen** for numeric ranges: `3-7 days`, `$$-$$$`
- **"N/A"** or **"Varies"** for empty table cells, never `—`

Shared trust line: import from `@/lib/editorial-copy` (`EDITORIAL_COPY.trustLine`).

Code comments should also avoid em/en dashes; use commas or periods.
